WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.380 --> 00:00:03.780
TERRY RYAN: Let's launch a
PHP application on App Engine

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:06.370
flexible environment.

00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:08.630
I have a simple Hello
World PHP application.

00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:10.610
I can run it locally
or in Docker,

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:14.481
but now we want to
run it on App Engine.

00:00:14.481 --> 00:00:15.980
The first thing I
need to do is sign

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:19.320
into Google Cloud Platform.

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:23.079
Once I sign in, I need
to create a new project.

00:00:23.079 --> 00:00:25.370
Now that I have my project,
I need to go Compute Engine

00:00:25.370 --> 00:00:27.526
and make sure
billing is enabled.

00:00:27.526 --> 00:00:29.900
Now I need to initialize the
project on my computer using

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:30.530
GCloud init.

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:33.640
It If you do not
have the Google Cloud

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:36.557
SDK installed on your computer,
download it from our website.

00:00:36.557 --> 00:00:38.890
Now we need to create an app
[? EML ?] file to configure

00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:40.879
this application on App Engine.

00:00:40.879 --> 00:00:42.670
Make sure to point App
Engine to the folder

00:00:42.670 --> 00:00:44.800
where it can find
your application.

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:46.450
In our case, it's in web.

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:49.280
Once that is done, deploy the
App Engine using the command

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:51.280
GCloud app deploy.

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:53.950
First time deployment
may take a few minutes.

00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:56.620
Now the application is up and
running with PHP on App Engine

00:00:56.620 --> 00:00:59.160
flexible environment.

